1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:05,636
每当你打开一个网站时，浏览器内部就开始了一场无声的战斗。
Every time you open a website, a silent battle starts inside your browser.

2
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:12,240
数十家公司在竞相加载广告、追踪你的点击，并建立你的个人画像。
Dozens of companies race to load ads, track your clicks, and build a profile of who you are.

3
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,644
紧接着，在几毫秒内，有些东西阻止了它们中的绝大部分。
And then, in a few milliseconds, something stops almost all of them.

4
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:19,120
这个东西就是广告拦截器。
That something is an ad blocker.

5
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,280
今天我们要深入探讨一下。
Today we are going deep.

6
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:23,840
广告拦截器到底是怎么工作的？
How do ad blockers actually work?

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,600
像 Brave 这样的浏览器是如何拦截广告的，甚至包括 YouTube 上的广告？
How does a browser like Brave block ads, even on YouTube?

8
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:31,520
人工智能又在如何改变这场对抗？
And how is artificial intelligence changing the fight?

9
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:33,028
让我们拆开来看看内部构造。
Let's open the hood.

10
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:39,300
首先，我们需要了解网页加载时到底发生了什么。
First, we need to understand what really happens when a web page loads.

11
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,880
你输入一个地址。
You type an address.

12
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:45,604
你的浏览器向网站服务器请求一个文件，也就是 HTML。
Your browser asks the website's server for one file, the HTML.

13
00:00:46,190 --> 00:00:48,720
但那个 HTML 只是一个配方。
But that HTML is just a recipe.

14
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:55,172
它告诉浏览器去获取更多内容，比如样式表、字体、图片和 JavaScript。
It tells the browser to fetch more things, style sheets, fonts, images, JavaScript.

15
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,308
其中一些文件来自网站本身。
Some of those files come from the website itself.

16
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,200
我们称之为第一方请求。
We call those first-party requests.

17
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:04,080
但许多请求来自完全不同的公司。
But many come from completely different companies.

18
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:10,116
广告网络、分析工具、社交媒体插件，这些都是第三方请求。
Ad networks, analytics tools, social media widgets, these are third-party requests.

19
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:20,000
一篇新闻文章可能会触发一百多个这样的请求，而每一个请求都是广告行业可以进入的门户。
A single news article can trigger more than a hundred of these requests,
and every one of them is a door the ad industry can walk through.

20
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:24,000
那么，在这些广告门户后面发生了什么？
So what happens behind one of those ad doors?

21
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:29,920
当页面为广告预留空间时，脚本会向广告交易平台发送请求。
When the page reserves a space for an ad, a script sends a request to an ad exchange.

22
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:32,400
交易平台会发起一场拍卖。
The exchange shouts out an auction.

23
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:37,028
这里有一位访客，这是我们掌握的关于他们的信息，谁想展示广告？
Here is a visitor, here is what we know about them, who wants to show an ad.

24
00:01:37,774 --> 00:01:40,000
广告主进行实时竞价。
Advertisers bid in real time.

25
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:43,204
获胜者的广告被发回并绘制在你的屏幕上。
The winner's ad is sent back and drawn on your screen.

26
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:50,720
整个拍卖过程通常在页面加载完成前的一瞬间就结束了。
This entire auction usually finishes in a fraction of a second before the page even finishes loading.

27
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:59,076
为了让这些竞价更智能，追踪脚本和不可见的 1 像素图像会跟随你穿梭于各个网站，收集数据。
To make those bids smarter, tracking scripts and invisible 1-pixel images follow you from site to site, collecting data.

28
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:06,148
所以，广告拦截器实际上是在同时对抗两个敌人：你能看到的广告和你看不见的追踪器。
So an ad blocker is really fighting two enemies at once, the ads you can see and the trackers you can't.

29
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:10,050
第一种武器是过滤列表。
Weapon number one, filter lists.

30
00:02:10,606 --> 00:02:15,204
过滤列表是一个巨大的、由大众维护的、包含各种规则的文本文件。
A filter list is a giant, crowd-maintained text file full of rules.

31
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:20,516
最著名的包括用于拦截广告的 EasyList 和用于拦截追踪器的 Easy Privacy。
The most famous ones are EasyList for ads and easy privacy for trackers.

32
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:30,080
一条规则可能很简单，比如拦截来自这个广告域名的所有内容，
或者拦截任何包含 slash ad slash banner 的地址。
A rule can be as simple as block anything from this advertising domain, or block any address that contains slash ad slash banner.

33
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:35,876
在你的浏览器发送请求之前，广告拦截器会根据这些规则检查地址。
Before your browser sends a request, the ad blocker checks the address against these rules.

34
00:02:36,334 --> 00:02:38,360
如果匹配成功，请求就会被取消。
If it matches, the request is cancelled.

35
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,388
它根本不会离开你的电脑。
It never leaves your computer.

36
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:43,204
没有下载，没有竞价，也没有追踪。
No download, no auction, no tracking.

37
00:02:43,726 --> 00:02:45,700
但这里有一个工程上的难题。
But here is the engineering problem.

38
00:02:46,222 --> 00:02:51,780
这些列表包含成千上万条规则，而一个页面会发出数百个请求。
These lists hold tens of thousands of rules, and a page fires hundreds of requests.

39
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:56,132
如果对每个请求都去匹配每一条规则，速度会慢到令人难以忍受。
Checking every rule against every request would be painfully slow.

40
00:02:56,686 --> 00:03:03,684
因此，现代引擎会将每个地址分解成小的标记，就像单词一样，并将规则保存在索引中。
So modern engines break each address into small tokens, like words, and keep the rules in an index.

41
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,960
对于每个请求，它们只测试共享相同标记的那几条规则。
For each request, they only test the handful of rules that share a token.

42
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:14,000
这就是为什么检查只需微秒，而不是毫秒的原因。
This is how the check takes microseconds instead of milliseconds.

43
00:03:15,118 --> 00:03:17,892
但拦截请求只是完成了一半的工作。
But blocking the request is only half the job.

44
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:22,240
页面上仍然有一个原本该放广告的空白框。
The page still has an empty box where the ad was supposed to be.

45
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:25,412
有时候甚至还会显示「广告」字样。
Sometimes it even says, advertisement.

46
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:28,640
这就是外观过滤派上用场的地方。
This is where cosmetic filtering comes in.

47
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:32,080
外观规则不会拦截网络流量。
Cosmetic rules don't block network traffic.

48
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:38,948
它们针对页面本身的部分，使用与 Web 开发人员相同的 CSS 选择器。
They target pieces of the page itself, using the same CSS selectors web developers use.

49
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:45,732
像「隐藏所有 class 为 ad banner 的元素」这样的规则，会告诉浏览器折叠那个框。
A rule like Hide every element with the class ad banner tells the browser to collapse that box.

50
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:51,328
周围的内容会向上滑动，页面看起来就像从来没有出现过广告一样。
The surrounding content slides up, and the page looks like the ad was never there.

51
00:03:52,528 --> 00:03:56,644
第三种武器在更深的一层运作，那就是 DNS 拦截。
Weapon number three works one level deeper, DNS blocking.

52
00:03:57,166 --> 00:04:02,948
在你的设备与任何服务器通信之前，它必须查找该地址，就像查电话簿一样。
Before your device can talk to any server, it has to look up its address, like checking a phone book.

53
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:05,636
这种查找被称为 DNS。
That lookup is called DNS.

54
00:04:06,126 --> 00:04:12,128
DNS 拦截器就像你家庭网络上的一个过滤孔，它只是对广告域名撒谎。
A DNS blocker, like a pie hole on your home network, simply lies about ad domains.

55
00:04:12,368 --> 00:04:15,408
当有东西请求广告服务器时，它会给出一个答案。
When something asks for an ad server, it answers.

56
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,156
那个地址根本去不了任何地方。
That address goes nowhere.

57
00:04:17,488 --> 00:04:20,676
最棒的一点是，它能同时保护所有设备。
The great thing is that it protects every device at once.

58
00:04:21,038 --> 00:04:25,476
你的手机、智能电视，甚至是那些不是浏览器的 App。
Your phone, your smart TV, even apps that aren't browsers.

59
00:04:25,934 --> 00:04:29,808
但广告商用一种叫 CNAME 伪装的手段反击了过来。
But advertisers fought back with a trick called CNAME cloaking.

60
00:04:29,968 --> 00:04:34,468
他们把追踪器隐藏在网站本身看似无害的子域名后面。
They hide a tracker behind a harmless-looking subdomain of the website itself.

61
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:43,888
更智能的拦截器，包括 Brave 在内，会追踪这个别
名链到真实的终点，揭开追踪器的伪装并将其拦截。
Smarter blockers, Brave included, follow that alias chain to the real destination, uncloak the tracker, and block it anyway.

62
00:04:45,198 --> 00:04:46,756
现在我们来聊聊 Brave。
Now let's talk about Brave.

63
00:04:47,502 --> 00:04:50,048
大多数广告拦截器都是插件。
Most ad blockers are extensions.

64
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:54,724
它们运行在浏览器之上，请求浏览器权限来检查流量。
They sit on top of the browser and ask it for permission to inspect traffic.

65
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:56,644
Brave 走了一条不同的路线。
Brave took a different route.

66
00:04:57,166 --> 00:05:01,728
它的拦截器叫 Shields，是直接内置在浏览器里的。
Its blocker, called Shields, is built directly into the browser itself.

67
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:07,524
Shields 背后的引擎是用 Rust 编写的，这是一种快速且内存安全的语言。
The engine behind Shields is written in Rust, a fast and memory-safe language.

68
00:05:08,014 --> 00:05:14,692
Brave 用 Rust 重构了它，并报告说它的运行速度比之前的版本快了大约 69 倍。
Brave rebuilt it in Rust and reported it running about 69 times faster than their previous version.

69
00:05:15,246 --> 00:05:24,900
它读取与 AdBlock Plus 和 UBlock Origin 相同的过滤列表语
法，因此它受益于多年的社区工作，再加上 Brave 自己的列表。
It reads the same filter list syntax as AdBlock Plus and UBlock Origin,
so it benefits from years of community work, plus Brave's own lists.

70
00:05:25,422 --> 00:05:38,928
而且因为 Shields 是浏览器的一部分，而不是插件，所以它不受 Chrome 新版插件规则（即
Manifest Version 3）的限制，那些规则限制了插件过滤流量的能力。
And because Shields is part of the browser, not an extension, it is not limited by Chrome's newer extension rules,
known as Manifest Version 3, which put caps on how extensions can filter traffic.

71
00:05:39,168 --> 00:05:48,608
网络拦截、外观过滤、CNAME 去伪装以及防指纹识别，都在页面渲染之前协同工作。
Network blocking, cosmetic filtering, CNAME uncloaking, and anti-fingerprinting all work together before the page even paints.

72
00:05:49,568 --> 00:05:51,568
现在是最终 Boss：YouTube。
Now the boss level, YouTube.

73
00:05:52,288 --> 00:05:54,788
在 YouTube 上，经典的手段就失效了。
On YouTube, the classic trick fails.

74
00:05:55,182 --> 00:06:00,580
广告和视频来自同一家公司，通常甚至来自同一个服务器。
Ads and videos are served from the same company, often from the very same servers.

75
00:06:00,848 --> 00:06:04,128
拦截广告域名，你也就把视频也给拦截了。
Block the ad domain, and you block the video too.

76
00:06:04,368 --> 00:06:06,688
所以拦截器转向了页面内部。
So blockers moved inside the page.

77
00:06:06,990 --> 00:06:09,188
它们使用被称为 scriplets 的微型脚本。
They use tiny scripts called scriplets.

78
00:06:09,728 --> 00:06:11,140
聪明的地方就在这里。
Here is the clever part.

79
00:06:11,488 --> 00:06:16,580
在视频开始前，YouTube 播放器会接收到一段描述视频的数据块。
Before a video starts, the YouTube player receives a block of data describing the video.

80
00:06:17,102 --> 00:06:22,528
这些数据中包含一个广告位列表，说明广告何时播放以及播放哪些广告。
Inside that data is a list of ad slots, when ads should play and which ones.

81
00:06:22,958 --> 00:06:28,164
一个 scriplet 会拦截这些数据，并在播放器读取之前删除广告字段。
A scriptlet intercepts that data and deletes the ad fields before the player reads them.

82
00:06:28,608 --> 00:06:33,248
像广告投放和播放器广告之类的字段就直接消失了。
Fields with names like ad placements and player ads simply vanish.

83
00:06:33,646 --> 00:06:39,008
播放器查看数据，发现没有预定的广告，于是就直接播放你的视频。
The player looks at the data, sees no ads scheduled, and plays your video straight away.

84
00:06:39,248 --> 00:06:41,488
当然，YouTube 也会反击。
Of course, YouTube fights back.

85
00:06:41,648 --> 00:06:47,844
它增加了检测代码来检查广告是否被移除，并显示警告或阻止播放。
It adds detection code that checks whether ads were removed and shows a warning or blocks playback.

86
00:06:48,398 --> 00:06:52,448
拦截器则用新的 scriplets 来应对，这些脚本能躲过那项检测。
Blockers respond with new scriplets that hide from that detection.

87
00:06:52,846 --> 00:06:59,728
正是这种猫鼠游戏，导致 YouTube 的过滤列表有时一天更新好几次。
This cat and mouse game is why filter lists for YouTube are updated sometimes several times a day.

88
00:07:00,688 --> 00:07:05,892
而 YouTube 最新的招式是最难对付的：服务端广告插入。
And YouTube's newest move is the hardest one yet: server-side ad insertion.

89
00:07:06,414 --> 00:07:12,996
服务器不再把广告作为独立的视频发送，而是直接把广告缝合到视频流本身中。
Instead of sending the ad as a separate video, the server stitches the ad directly into the video stream itself.

90
00:07:13,614 --> 00:07:17,892
对于你的浏览器来说，它全都是一段连续的视频分片流。
To your browser, it is all one continuous stream of video chunks.

91
00:07:18,318 --> 00:07:22,756
这里没有独立的广告文件可以拦截，也没有可以过滤的广告域名。
There is no separate ad file to block and no ad domain to filter.

92
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:25,408
拦截器仍然可以寻找蛛丝马迹。
Blockers can still look for clues.

93
00:07:25,648 --> 00:07:33,092
播放器通常需要知道广告从哪里开始以及持续多久，因此这些时间数据就成了新的目标。
The player usually needs to know where the ad starts and how long it lasts, so that timing data becomes the new target.

94
00:07:33,646 --> 00:07:43,044
至于创作者亲自读的赞助信息，像 sponsor block
这样的工具利用众包的时间戳来自动跳过这些片段。
And for sponsor messages that creators read themselves, tools like sponsor
block use crowdsourced timestamps to skip those segments automatically.

95
00:07:43,566 --> 00:07:51,648
但这正是仅靠规则开始失效的地方，这就引出了人工智能。
But this is exactly the kind of problem where rules alone start to break down, which brings us to artificial intelligence.

96
00:07:52,608 --> 00:07:56,388
过滤列表有一个巨大的弱点：它们是人类编写的。
Filter lists have one big weakness humans write them.

97
00:07:56,846 --> 00:08:02,288
当出现新的广告网络时，必须有人注意到它，编写规则，然后发布更新。
When a new ad network appears, someone has to notice it, write a rule, and ship an update.

98
00:08:02,448 --> 00:08:04,448
机器学习改变了这种逻辑。
Machine learning flips this around.

99
00:08:05,006 --> 00:08:10,816
它不再询问“这个地址在列表上吗？”，而是询问“这看起来和表现起来像广告吗？”
Instead of asking, is this address on a list, it asks, does this look and behave like an ad?

100
00:08:11,136 --> 00:08:14,176
第一种方法：像人类一样识别广告。
Approach one, seeing ads like a human.

101
00:08:14,416 --> 00:08:19,044
来自 Brave 和合作大学的研究人员构建了一个名为 Percival 的系统。
Researchers from Brave and partner universities built a system called Percival.

102
00:08:19,456 --> 00:08:25,988
Percival 在浏览器的图像渲染管道中放入了一个紧凑的卷积神经网络。
Percival places a compact convolutional neural network inside the browser's image rendering pipeline.

103
00:08:26,670 --> 00:08:32,256
每张图片在到达你的屏幕之前，都会被分类为广告或非广告。
Every image is classified as ad or not ad before it reaches your screen.

104
00:08:32,496 --> 00:08:44,576
在他们发布的测试中，它的决策与 EasyList 匹配的比例约为 97%，
甚至能识别出列表难以处理的社交媒体原生赞助贴。
In their published tests, it matched easy list decisions about 97% of the time, and
even caught first-party sponsored posts on social media that lists struggle with.

105
00:08:44,878 --> 00:08:47,364
第二种方法：追踪线索。
Approach 2, following the clues.

106
00:08:47,616 --> 00:08:51,776
一个名为 Ad Graph 的系统构建了整个页面的图谱。
A system called Ad Graph builds a graph of the entire page.

107
00:08:52,016 --> 00:09:00,016
每个 HTML 元素、每个脚本和每个网络请求都变成一个节点，而边则显示谁创建了什么。
Every HTML element, every script, and every network request becomes a node, and the edges show who created what.

108
00:09:00,398 --> 00:09:04,644
机器学习分类器随后研究这个关系网。
A machine learning classifier then studies that web of relationships.

109
00:09:05,038 --> 00:09:14,244
一个由广告脚本加载、创建 iframe、并调用追踪服务器的脚本会被标记，即使它的地址是全新的。
A script that was loaded by an ad script that creates an if-frame, that
calls a tracking server, gets flagged, even if its address is brand new.

110
00:09:14,958 --> 00:09:23,204
Ad Graph 以约 95% 的准确率重现了过滤列表的决策，并发现了列表本身中的错误。
Ad Graph reproduced filter list decisions with about 95% accuracy and found mistakes in the lists themselves.

111
00:09:23,630 --> 00:09:24,580
第三种方法。
Approach 3.

112
00:09:25,006 --> 00:09:26,212
阅读和倾听。
Reading and listening.

113
00:09:26,766 --> 00:09:32,772
语言模型可以识别伪装成普通文章的赞助文本和原生广告。
Language models can spot sponsored text and native ads that are disguised as normal articles.

114
00:09:33,102 --> 00:09:41,376
对于视频，模型可以分析转录文本、音频和场景变化，以找出广告片段的开始和结束位置。
And for video, models can analyze transcripts, audio, and scene changes to find where an ad segment begins and ends.

115
00:09:41,616 --> 00:09:45,508
在实践中，最强大的系统结合了所有这些方法。
In practice, the strongest systems combine all of these.

116
00:09:46,062 --> 00:09:55,364
快速规则在微秒内处理已知威胁，而 AI 模型则帮助发现新威胁，
通常是通过为列表建议新规则来实现。
Fast rules handle the known threats in microseconds, and AI models help
discover the new ones, often by suggesting new rules for the lists.

117
00:09:57,326 --> 00:10:00,228
让我们把所有内容整合起来，按广告类型分类。
Let's put it all together, ad type by ad type.

118
00:10:00,816 --> 00:10:08,708
横幅和展示广告，通过过滤列表在网络层面拦截，并利用外观规则清理空白区域。
Banner and display ads, blocked at the network level by filter lists, with cosmetic rules cleaning up the empty space.

119
00:10:08,976 --> 00:10:15,972
弹窗和弹出式广告，通过阻止打开它们的脚本以及通过浏览器的弹窗保护来拦截。
Pop-ups and pop-undares, blocked by stopping the scripts that open them, and by browser pop-up protection.

120
00:10:16,526 --> 00:10:24,900
追踪像素和分析工具，通过 Easy Privacy 等隐私列表、DNS 拦截和 CNAME 去伪装来拦截。
Tracking pixels and analytics, blocked by privacy lists like Easy Privacy, DNS blocking, and CNAME uncloaking.

121
00:10:25,454 --> 00:10:33,156
YouTube 的片头和片中广告，是通过 scriplets 在
播放器调度广告之前就把广告数据删掉来处理的。
YouTube pre-roll and mid-roll ads, handled by scriplets that remove ad data from the player before it can schedule them.

122
00:10:33,742 --> 00:10:38,212
原生广告和赞助贴更难处理，因为它们就在同一个网站上。
Native and sponsored posts, harder because they live on the same site.

123
00:10:38,736 --> 00:10:42,852
这里需要依靠外观规则，以及 AI 视觉或语言模型来辅助。
Cosmetic rules and AI vision or language models help here.

124
00:10:43,438 --> 00:10:45,856
嵌入式视频广告和赞助商读条。
Stitched in video ads and sponsor reads.

125
00:10:46,190 --> 00:10:52,804
这是目前的边界，正在测试时间数据、众包片段以及机器学习检测。
The frontier, where timing data, crowdsource segments, and machine learning detection are being tested.

126
00:10:54,016 --> 00:10:55,204
最后再说一点。
One last thought.

127
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:58,884
广告是许多网站和创作者支付账单的方式。
ads are how many websites and creators pay their bills.

128
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:09,380
拦截广告是一种选择，很多人通过直接支持创作者、购买去广告套餐，
或者允许自己喜欢的网站展示广告来平衡这一点。
Blocking them is a choice, and many people balance it by supporting creators
directly, paying for ad-free plans, or allowing ads on sites they love.

129
00:11:09,856 --> 00:11:14,852
但了解广告拦截的原理，就意味着理解现代互联网是如何运作的。
But understanding how ad blocking works means understanding how the modern web works.

130
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:20,416
请求、脚本、竞价、数据，以及现在的人工智能。
Requests, scripts, auctions, data, and now artificial intelligence.

131
